# SABOTAGE: UXD-05 attempt-4 (`_orch/verify/T11-verdict-attempt3.json`, V11's REFUTATION of
# attempt 3's `33723d8`; ADR-047 §10a row 19) — `alias_env/1`'s prewalk stops matching
# `{:require, _, args}`, so Elixir's OTHER alias-creating form binds nothing again:
# `require Samen.AI.Agent, as: A` then `A.start(...)` (and the prefix, apply/3 and
# require-seeded-chain variants) evade the F-4 raw-spawn lock. V11 proved this AT THE GATE,
# not just at the predicate: `spawn_lock_violations/2` returned 0 for a require-as fixture
# against 1 for a byte-identical plain-`alias` control. Plain `alias` renames, chains and
# parent-namespace renames are UNAFFECTED: this patch reopens only the `require ..., as:`
# class. (`require_bindings/1` goes unused under this patch — a warning, not an error.)
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/ai/agent_coverage_verifier_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: RED FIXTURE (UXD-05, attempt 4) — `require ..., as:` renaming the KERNEL evades the DIRECT-CALL form
# MUST_FAIL: RED FIXTURE (UXD-05, attempt 4) — `require ..., as:` evades the apply/3 form
# MUST_FAIL: RED FIXTURE (UXD-05, attempt 4) — `require ..., as:` renaming a PREFIX segment
# MUST_FAIL: RED FIXTURE (UXD-05, attempt 4) — a require-as binding SEEDS a further alias chain
# MUST_FAIL: spawn_lock_violations/2 flips on the require-as and atom-alias fixture paths (refutable, gate level)
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/mix/tasks/samen.verify.agent_coverage.ex b/samen_core/lib/mix/tasks/samen.verify.agent_coverage.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/mix/tasks/samen.verify.agent_coverage.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/mix/tasks/samen.verify.agent_coverage.ex
@@ -273,7 +273,6 @@
     {_ast, bindings} =
       Macro.prewalk(ast, [], fn
         {:alias, _, args} = node, acc when is_list(args) -> {node, alias_bindings(args) ++ acc}
-        {:require, _, args} = node, acc when is_list(args) -> {node, require_bindings(args) ++ acc}
         node, acc -> {node, acc}
       end)
 
